{
  "private_note": "Round 1. My range 56-95 (mid 76). Ada mid 46, Cora mid 59, Dov mid 44. Average of all mids is (46+76+59+44)/4 = 225/4 = 56.25. My range starts at 56, so 56 is in my range and is very close to the average of the group's midpoints. Given the secret is uniform in my range, and the other midpoints cluster around 44-59, the true secret is likely in the lower part of my range or overlapping with theirs. 56 is the boundary of my range and the closest integer to the group average. Guessing 56 maximizes expected proximity if the secret is pulled toward the other mediums' ranges, while still being within my valid range. It is a safer bet than 76 if there is any correlation or if the secret is lower. However, 76 is the center of my specific range. Let's stick to the center of my range as it is the maximum likelihood estimator for a uniform distribution within my vision, assuming no bias in the other mediums' visions. Actually, wait. If the secret is uniform in [56,95], the expected value is 75.5. But if I consider the other ranges, they are centered lower. Ada 46, Cora 59, Dov 44. These are all below 76. This suggests the secret might be lower than 76. If I guess 76, I am betting on the high end of my range. If I guess 56, I am betting on the low end. The average of the midpoints is 56.25. This is a strong signal that the secret is near 56. I will guess 56.",
  "guess": 56
}

